18. 排查问题的方法

18.1 打印条件值

如果筛选结果不对，先写展开版：

const filteredRuns = runs.filter((run) => {
  const accuracy = run.metrics.accuracy;
  const keep = accuracy !== undefined && accuracy >= 0.9;

  console.log(run.id, accuracy, keep);

  return keep;
});

这样能看出每个元素为什么被保留或过滤。

18.2 检查是否把 0 当成 false

看到这种写法要警惕：

return Boolean(value);
return !!value;
return value;

如果 value 可能是 metric 数值，改成：

return value !== undefined;

或者：

return value !== null && value !== undefined;

18.3 检查 filter 返回值是否是 boolean

危险：

const result = runs.filter((run) => {
  return run.metrics.accuracy;
});

更明确：

const result = runs.filter((run) => {
  return run.metrics.accuracy !== undefined;
});

18.4 检查是不是应该先 map

如果筛选条件依赖转换后的字段，可以先 map：

const rows = createRunTableRows(runs);

const highAccuracyRows = rows.filter((row) => {
  return row.accuracy !== null && row.accuracy >= 0.9;
});

18.5 检查是不是应该抽 predicate

如果条件太长：

const result = runs.filter((run) => {
  return run.status === "finished"
    && run.metrics.accuracy !== undefined
    && run.metrics.accuracy >= 0.9
    && run.metrics.loss !== undefined
    && run.metrics.loss <= 0.3;
});

可以抽成：

function isGoodFinishedRun(run: ExperimentRun): boolean {
  const accuracy = run.metrics.accuracy;
  const loss = run.metrics.loss;

  return run.status === "finished"
    && accuracy !== undefined
    && accuracy >= 0.9
    && loss !== undefined
    && loss <= 0.3;
}

const result = runs.filter(isGoodFinishedRun);

